{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492305-a-space-opera-book","id":1492305,"title":"A Space Opera Book!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-04T09:14:22-07:00","id":1492305,"title":"A Space Opera Book!","content":"What it says on the tin. I want a Space Opera Book for the WoD. It would be mainly an alternative reality set up. <br /> <br /> Mages are perfect for Space Opera, Changelings would delight in it. Garou and other Fera would adapt, with the Corax and the Ratkin truly loving it. Wraiths could be lost in space as well as anyplace else. Vampires would be freaked by Space, which would be fun too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T21:51:56-07:00","id":1492414,"title":"","content":"<br /> Hmm.....<br /> <br /> Maybe start with the three factions who would work best at it: The Sons of Ether Ethernauts, the Nockers \u00c6thernauts, and the Glasswalker Umbral Flyers*.<br /> <br /> With those three as the base, this would be something that draws heavily on Victorian scientific romance and science fiction (see the old Space 1889 RPG) and pulp era science fantasy (John Carter and others). For those who traffic in the World(s) Beyond, our solar system is a place of endless wonder and adventure. The Moon, Venus, and Mars are the mysterious caverns, lush jungles, and canal-crossed deserts of fiction and imagination, with their own native inhabitants. Even Mercury has a thin belt of life on the border between the molten sunside and the frozen dark. Hidden on the other side of the sun is the haunted machine world of Vulcan. The many moons of Jupiter and Saturn are mysterious new worlds in their own right. Uranus is a world of never-ending sky and Neptune the ultimate sea. Pluto holds its own secrets, including outposts for invaders from the Dark Between the Stars.<br /> <br /> Mage, Fae, and Shifter heroes travel these worlds in their self built ships (think more akin to the Millenium Falcon or Serenity than giant star cruisers), wielding laser swords, psychic blasters, and lens crystals. <br /> <br /> Anyway, that would be my basic pitch.<br /> <br /> *(The Umbral Flyers were the main rivals of the Wise Guys for tribal leadership in the 30s and 40s, essentially aviators, science heroes, and pulp adventures/explorers. By the 70s, they'd largely faded into the sunset, save a handful of Umbral explorers. Dr. Stratus, part of Vic Stryker's group in the revised Silent Striders book and Past Lives, was one of their leading lights.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T22:59:42-07:00","id":1492418,"title":"","content":"Vampires shun space travel, as Uranus is famously infested with werewolves.<br /> <br /> (Backs away and out the door)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T23:31:21-07:00","id":1492419,"title":"","content":"Wraiths would be rarely seen somewhat baroque looking ghost ships piloted by Harbingers and/or Ferrymen. The subterranean tunnels of the Moon sometimes connect to The Labyrinth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T23:34:08-07:00","id":1492420,"title":"","content":"There is a secret colony of Lasombra on the dark side of the Moon. How they got there is a mystery. They subsist on their human ghoul retainers and lunar natives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T06:36:39-07:00","id":1492427,"title":"","content":"If there was some sort of Space Base (not that there already is), would it be an extension of the Dark Kingdom of Iron or would the souls make a new Dark Kingdom? I really like the name 'The Dark Kingdom of Dust' for a lunar/space underworld.<br /> <br /> Changeling (particular Sidhe) I feel would have a weird reverence to the moon. It was the original moon landing that was the start of Resurgence. I can see original location of the landing be something people make pilgrimages to (maybe even being the only Glade on the moon).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T07:25:43-07:00","id":1492428,"title":"","content":"This also just came to me. I would think Fera/Garou that where born on the moon would secede themselves from the Nation and make their own ALA Newtypes and Beast Court. Maybe get a different name for themselves and make new strange spirit contracts/gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T07:58:37-07:00","id":1492430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492305-a-space-opera-book#post1492305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it says on the tin. I want a Space Opera Book for the WoD. It would be mainly an alternative reality set up.<br /> <br /> Mages are perfect for Space Opera, Changelings would delight in it. Garou and other Fera would adapt, with the Corax and the Ratkin truly loving it. Wraiths could be lost in space as well as anyplace else. Vampires would be freaked by Space, which would be fun too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> AHA! I LOVE this.<br /> <br /> Awhile ago over at <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/Aaronsmonsters\" target=\"_blank\">my Patreon</a> I was tinkering around with something quite like this. Using the basic storyteller system to run pulpy space opera games. For a simple back story, I used the Cthulhu Mythos to stitch it all together, just so that players would have something to grab onto. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">At present I have the basic rules, character creation, some creatures, etc. I focus on mortals in this game, with some material dipping into Consor level characters such as Psychics, Bygones, etc, </span></span></span>but it would be easy enough to add Mages, Vampires and the like.<br /> <br /> This material is free BTW. But I appreciate subscribers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/mythos-space-vs-39589417\" target=\"_blank\">Mythos Space Intro</a> (Basic Rules, Character Creation and a Character Sheet)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/mythos-space-65296469\" target=\"_blank\">Strike Fighter</a> (a Combat starship)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/mythos-space-66209211\" target=\"_blank\">The Gloom Hunters</a> (Sample Characters)<br /> <br /> If interest is shown, I will delve more into this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-06-2022, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T15:42:59-07:00","id":1492458,"title":"","content":"MythAdvocate I went right to your links, but something makes the pages to wide and won't let me see the edges. So I couldn't read anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T17:57:27-07:00","id":1492470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492305-a-space-opera-book?p=1492458#post1492458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MythAdvocate I went right to your links, but something makes the pages to wide and won't let me see the edges. So I couldn't read anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is strange. When I follow the links, this is not the case. I don't think it is something on my end. But I will look into it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> Try it again. I shrunk the pixel width of the images. That should help it resize for mobile devices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":".  Addressing resize issues. 09-07-2022, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T01:28:43-07:00","id":1492492,"title":"","content":"Most Vampires avoid travel, of course, but they do live in well-funded colonies all across the system. Some social experiments towards their fabled Blood Utopia, secret dark retreats where undead cabals gather information mundane and arcane for whatever plans they have, hideouts for the spiders in the conspiracy webs within other communities, either in allegiance to local powers or against them.<br /> <br /> But with space-worthy tech it isn't hard to overcome Kindred limitations. Blocking light is an easier demand on a spacesuit than pressure control, yet both are a basic requirement anyway. Some Kindred vessels are luxurious fortresses purposefully badly illuminated, manned by Ghouls, Revenants and Conditioned mortals, others are as minimal as being just an escape module reconditioned for longer travel yet no life support whatsoever. Even the big ones are a dire prospect for invaders, as vampires can sacrifice any life-saving system and fill it with dangerous traps, making the entire ship a literal tomb with no risk to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T04:46:55-07:00","id":1492505,"title":"","content":"The Mythos Space setting uses the &quot;classic&quot; storyteller system, focusing on human and human+ level characters. Adding supernaturals from the WOD is easy as can be, and could fit quite well in the setting without much adjustment.<br /> <br /> You can find character creation rules, a basic rules booklet and a character sheet on my <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/Aaronsmonsters\" target=\"_blank\">patreon</a>, free of charge. Though I am greatly encouraged by patronage.<br /> <br /> This is the basic introduction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>MYTHOS SPACE</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://c10.patreonusercontent.com/4/patreon-media/p/post/39589417/89f96d9093574a729b622e4f7ef61f79/eyJyb3RhdGUiOjAsInciOjgyMCwid2VicCI6MH0%3D/1.jpg?token-time=1663804800&amp;token-hash=nA7bHuDDA9uwJ5RIJfNmLRHy1ekwmGfE6yVrbPjfTsE%3D\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>\u201cThe explorers and the drifters and the spacehands are misfits mostly, and, therefore, men of imagination. The contrast between the rigid functionalism inside a spaceship and the immeasurable glories outside is too great not to have a name. So whenever you stand in a ship\u2019s control room and look out into the bottomless dark where the blinding planets turn and the stars swim motionless in space, you are taking a walk down Paradise Street.\u201d</i> \u2015 <b>C.L. Moore,</b> <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/1977817\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Judgment Night</b></a><br /> A few years ago, I was tinkering with the Mythos Space concept as a kind of love letter to some of my favorite types of fiction, pulpy sci-fi, and cosmic horror. So while I am busy with other projects, I will also be posting about this setting, using the &quot;Classic&quot; World of Darkness game system, both due to its time tested nature and because it is fairly open source as you can find the rules info all over the internet. But to make things easier, I have attached a pdf of the basic rules, character creation rules and a character sheet below, and will be adding features as these articles progress. In the days to come, I will be discussing the setting, how it meshes with the Storyteller System, and eventually assemble a large pdf book that will be available to be downloaded. Members of this patreon will have access to a deluxe version, with artwork, fiction and other features.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>THE BASICS</b><br /> The setting of Mythos Space is a pulp science fantasy campaign inspired by comics such as Flash Gordon and Buck Rogers, and the Cosmic Horror stories of the Cthulhu Mythos<b>*</b>, and sci-fi movies and television shows from the 1950s and \u201860s such as Forbidden Planet, Outer Limits, Twilight Zone, and Captain Video. The focus is on fun, horror and excitement rather than scientific accuracy. Crazy retro gadgets, weird creatures, sexy alien princesses (or princes), and tentacled aliens are all par for the course.<br /> Space travel, ray guns and alien life is common knowledge and considered &quot;normal&quot; as far as Joe Average is concerned. But so is the existence of mind-shattering alien horrors, Deep Ones, Snake-People and all manner of weirdness. But most people try <i>very</i> hard to get on with their lives despite this.<br /> <b>*</b><span style=\"color:#000080\">This includes material from H.P. Lovecraft, Clark Ashton Smith, Robert E. Howard, C.S. Moore, Robert Bloch, Frank Belknap Long, Henry Kuttner, and Fritz Leiber.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>SOME SETTING TIDBITS</b><br /> Overall, the setting of Mythos Space has a &quot;retro future&quot; <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">where retro, vintage or antiquated technology, styles and aesthetics are still used, but which otherwise is or at least resembles the present day. This is largely due to the mix of tech levels available across settled space, and as a direct result of conflict with hyperspace entities (who can really screw with certain technologies). </span></span></span><br /> <b>Old Earth (Terra):</b> Earth is a ruin, and home to only small communities in the 51st century. Mankind has spread across the stars, leaving their homeworld behind and hoping to make a better future.<br /> <b>Space</b> <b>Patrol (Space Cops): </b>Space Patrol is a private security company that provides armed peacekeeping, investigative and security services to private and public clients in outer space. This organization originally got its start as a police force created by a collaboration between the United Americans and the Afro-European Union, but has since become a private corporation that acts as a police force in space. In the 51st century, the Space Patrol is central to space travel.<br /> <b>The Colonies</b> <b>(Separatists): </b>Colony worlds can be found across space, settled by corporations, private individuals and even hard-as-nails homesteaders looking for a new start. Most of the larger and more developed worlds were founded during the mass colonial efforts of Earth governments of the 23rd century. During this exodus from Terra, Spacecraft were still only capable of sub-light speeds at the time. Voyages beyond Earth\u2019s solar system took generations and the colonies that were established were effectively isolated from each other and from Terra. This forced the individual colonized star systems to be completely self-sufficient in all their vital requirements (food, medicine, technology, etc.) and allowed them to develop distinctive languages and cultures.<br /> <b>The Hyades Star Cluster</b> (Campaign): This is to be the main focus for my games. Mention of this region appears in the assorted Mythos, as well as UFO lore. It is a haunted region of space, with ancient ruins and some creepy locals. I will be centering on a colonized system that is close enough to Earth standards to be a good starting point.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-07-2022, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T11:04:32-07:00","id":1492533,"title":"","content":"Sorry, but I have to say that while it may be fitting for the works of the time, the split of Earth-related governments into US-like Corporate states and Totally-Not-China-Empire-of-Totalitarian-Totalitarianism is a big no for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T12:31:18-07:00","id":1492545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492305-a-space-opera-book?p=1492533#post1492533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but I have to say that while it may be fitting for the works of the time, the split of Earth-related governments into US-like Corporate states and Totally-Not-China-Empire-of-Totalitarian-Totalitarianism is a big no for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know. I agree with you. And I am going to remove that aspect. It is fine without inserting that sort of thing into the setting. I initially wanted to mix some Lovecraft, Delta Green and Dr. Who Earth History material in, but it all gets too charged with modern issues. And I don't want to get into that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Thank you for pointing that out. I want this to be fun. Not upset anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-07-2022, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T12:45:59-07:00","id":1492548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492305-a-space-opera-book?p=1492545#post1492545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know. I agree with you. And I am going to remove that aspect. It is fine without inserting that sort of thing into the setting. I initially wanted to mix some Lovecraft, Delta Green and Dr. Who Earth History material in, but it all gets too charged with modern issues. And I don't want to get into that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Thank you for pointing that out. I want this to be fun. Not upset anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI wonder if doing the Starfinder Golarion treatment for Terra would be better. &quot;Terra use to be here but it one day fell out of space-time and no one knows how or why. All information related to the event is under an anti-memetic field of some kind.&quot; I don't know if it would hackish or something intriguing to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T13:23:07-07:00","id":1492551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492305-a-space-opera-book?p=1492548#post1492548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI wonder if doing the Starfinder Golarion treatment for Terra would be better. &quot;Terra use to be here but it one day fell out of space-time and no one knows how or why. All information related to the event is under an anti-memetic field of some kind.&quot; I don't know if it would hackish or something intriguing to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the initial concept, when Rl'yeh rose, the resulting war effectively ruined the Earth. Though &quot;The Fishy Gods&quot; were repelled, it was at a terrible cost. Now the world is a blasted, polluted ruin that is locked in a never-ending Ice Age of filthy ice and poisoned ecology. Of course, there are still people here (and things that look like people). But it is a terrible place.<br /> <br /> If used in a WOD setting, I would say that all of the Time of Judgement's apocalyptic events all happened, and that mankind only knows that a great many monstrous entities rampaged all over the world. Antediluvians, Wyrm Beasts, True Magick Mecha, Fomorians and whatnot went hog wild. And humanity fought back. Now, the only civilization to be found are vampire ruled city states where the human cattle within are happy to not be out in the fomori and spirit haunted wastelands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-07-2022, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T13:35:32-07:00","id":1492553,"title":"","content":"In a WoD version it could also be that all Time of Judgement prophecies were wrong and even the known big baddies were actually small fries compared to the actual Old Gods of the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T17:50:59-07:00","id":1492565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492305-a-space-opera-book?p=1492553#post1492553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a WoD version it could also be that all Time of Judgement prophecies were wrong and even the known big baddies were actually small fries compared to the actual Old Gods of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>This works quite well for me. Cosmic monstrosities are always a joy to play with. And are meat and drink to a space opera.<br /> <br /> Ack! You have convinced me to delve more into this setting. I will post occasional tidbits here, but the bulk will be at my Patreon. Please swing by. I value your input. You have impressed me with your posts here and elsewhere on these forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T08:03:55-07:00","id":1492599,"title":"","content":"NEW ALEXANDRIA<br /> The planet of New Alexandria is a major player in the Mythos Space universe. The world is a Democracy that embraces both Dynamic and Technocratic viewpoints, and is welcoming to all seekers of knowledge and wisdom.<br /> <br /> <b>Planet Name:</b> New Alexandria (HD 283869 b)<br /> <b>Planet Type:</b> Cool Desert<br /> <b>Sector:</b> Hyades Star Cluster<br /> <b>System:</b> Dabaran (Gamma Tauri)<br /> <b>Atmosphere:</b> Thin<br /> <b>Gravity:</b> Terran<br /> <b>Day Length:</b> 21 hours<br /> <b>Year Length:</b> 180 days<br /> <b>Population:</b> 4m (80% Human, 8% Android, 7% Ophidian, 5% Other)<br /> <b>Government:</b> Democratic Scientocracy*<br /> <b>Tech Level:</b> Hyperspace.<br /> <br /> New Alexandria is a major hub for mankind in the 51st century, and home of the greatest minds in the known universe (according to them at least). It is a planet of academics, dreamers, innovators and free thinkers who seek to not only maintain human civilization, but to understand the deeper meaning of the cosmos. The brilliance and technological innovations of New Alexandria has made the planet very wealthy, with ambitious researchers encouraged to pursue profitable, and dangerous developments.<br /> The planet itself is a cool, desert world that has little indigenous life and thin but breathable atmosphere. Terran life exists almost entirely in New Alexandria\u2019s domed and buried cities, where innovative science has brought many Earth species to this ragged world. Robots and other automated systems produce the food, air and water needed for survival. Raw materials are either recycled, imported, or created outright via scientific innovation.<br /> New Alexandria maintains their own security forces, called Sentinels. These no-nonsense troops are mostly humans and androids, backed by robot muscle (along with some lab grown monsters). They maintain a fleet of warships and patrol cruisers, but also maintain cordial relations with Space Patrol.<br /> <br /> LOCATIONS OF NOTE<br /> A complete list of the many interesting places of note on this world is beyond the scope of this post. But here are a few highlights.<br /> <b>Olympias City:</b> The city of Olympias is the primary settlement on New Alexandrian and home of its leaders and top intellectuals. It is a city-sized \u201ccollege town\u201d with a focus on innovation, technology and inspiring new leaders in the \u201csacred sciences.\u201d The city is a glittering, Art Deco city with moving sidewalks, glittering spires, flying cars, and huge domed observatories are all features of this city of wonders. The Academy is a major aspect of the city, where intellectual development is pursued and the great thinkers of New Alexandria are revered and encouraged to shine. <br /> <b>The Grand Archive:</b> This massive structure is located in Olympias City, and is the largest collection of academic, technical and cultural material in the known universe. Many obscure, arcane and dangerous materials exist here <u>only</u> in physical form due to its tendency to attract hyperspatial entities. The Archive has been specially warded against Astral Projection and Psychoportation.<br /> <b>Citadel of Shining Accord:</b> This glittering, crystalline structure is located in Olympias City, and is the Embassy for representatives of the Council of Andromeda. It is a beautiful structure that brings to mind ancient Egyptian, Greek and Indian motifs, but has its own distinct presence. Two <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/mythos-space-65675360\" target=\"_blank\">Andromedans</a>, Limpang-Tung and Sirami are nearly always present. The Citadel offers classes in music, art, philosophy, and psychic powers.<br /> <b>Custodia:</b> The city of Custodia is home to the majority of specialized and manual laborers of New Alexandria, as well as the bulk of industry for the planet. It is very much a \u201cfactory town\u201d and fully embraces its role as the workers for the planet\u2019s dreamers. Much of Custodia is underground, and is designed with industry and efficiency in mind, but is not without entertainment or comfort.<br /> <b>Delos Starport (Beanstalk):</b> This space station is tethered to the planet to allow larger ships to dock and to maintain a buffer between visitors and the planet below. The stations space elevator down to the surface providing easy access. The station is a bustling port town, with only a small number of permanent residents.<br /> <b>Garden of Hish:</b> The Garden of Hish is a stone structure that is home of Hish, an Elderian recluse of great intellect and psychic power. The Garden itself imposes an aura of absolute silence to all who visit, in fact, no sound may be heard here due to its masters will. Hish is attended by a small number of \u201cpet\u201d Shoggoths and a dozen human and near human acolytes who seek psychic tutelage and enlightenment. <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>*Scientocracy</b> is an ideology which advocates for government and public policy based on scientific evidence and/or of the opinions of scientists and experts. It is distinct from Technocracy, which is the <i>rule</i> of scientists and experts. In the Mythos Space setting, mankind has had many up close and personal encounters with supernatural entities. And so the sciences of New Alexandria are not nearly as rigid as they are in the classic World of Darkness. Many Tradition type mages and Technocrats are comfortable here.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-09-2022, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T08:18:00-07:00","id":1492601,"title":"","content":"I think that there is one for CoD in Mirrors","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}